## A single matte Disk, partial thetamax, alone under a distant
## light -- no shadow falls on it, so this fixture is safe to reuse for
## shadow-related fixtures too.
Display "r5a_disk.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 320 240 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
# Explicit, not the RI_EPSILON-near default: a flat, camera-facing disk is
# exactly the shape the near-clip precision defect corrupts hardest
# (AGENTS.md, "Flat or z-narrow geometry needs Clipping 0.5 50").
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
## The disk's normal is (0, 0, -1) (GMANDisk::getNormal); "from"/"to" below
## place the light so the direction toward it has a strong -z component
## (travel from [1 1 -5] to [0 0 0] is (-1, -1, 5), i.e. +z; the direction
## toward the light is the negation of that), reaching that face nearly
## head-on (N.L ~ 0.96) instead of grazing it.
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.1]
LightSource "distantlight" 2 "intensity" [1.0] "lightcolor" [1 1 1]
	"from" [1 1 -5] "to" [0 0 0]
Sides 2
Surface "matte" "Ka" [0.3] "Kd" [0.8]
Disk 0 1.5 270
WorldEnd
